# FR-R3-090 (SUP-01) — the local install matches the hardened CI install by
# default, rather than by a contributor remembering a flag.
#
# Every job in .github/workflows/full-gate.yml, ci.yml and pr.yml installs with
# `npm ci --ignore-scripts`. Without this file a contributor's plain `npm ci`
# runs third-party lifecycle scripts, so the tree that is scanned, linted and
# tested in CI was installed differently from the tree a contributor runs — and
# the contributor's was the less hardened of the two. It is also the one that
# runs an uncontained agent CLI.
#
# WHAT THIS BREAKS, and it is this repository's own script rather than a
# dependency's: package.json declares
#   "postinstall": "npm --prefix webview-ui install --no-audit --no-fund"
# With scripts off it no longer runs, so `webview-ui/node_modules` is not
# populated by `npm ci` alone. That is not a regression to work around — CI has
# always worked this way and compensates with an explicit second install. The
# same explicit command is now a DECLARED step in CONTRIBUTING.md, per the
# FR-R3-065 rule that a prerequisite hidden inside a gate is not the same as a
# declared one.
#
# tests/lint/install-flag-parity.test.ts fails when this file and the workflows'
# install flags disagree. Two authorities on one policy is the recurring defect;
# they now check against each other.
ignore-scripts=true
